# Automation Exercise — project overview

Playwright TypeScript tests target **`https://www.automationexercise.com`** (override with `BASE_URL`).

## Layout

- `src/ui/pages/*.page.ts` — Page Objects (locators first, methods + assertions below).
- `src/ui/fixtures.ts` — Custom `test` wiring fixtures (no PageManager).
- `src/ui/data-providers/*.ts` — UI test data; import strings from `@utils/constants`.
- `src/api/services/*.ts` — API calls + assertions; specs use fixtures, not raw `request`.
- `src/api/data-providers/*.ts` — API scenario data.
- `src/tests/ui/*.spec.ts` — UI flows only; use `withStepContext` for clearer failures.
- `src/tests/api/*.spec.ts` — API flows only.
- `src/utils/constants.ts` — Shared literals and patterns.

## Spec layer (read before writing any test)

- `docs/requirements.md` — the requirements baseline (`REQ-*`) for the site under test.
- `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md` — behaviour contracts derived from it.
- `openspec/AGENTS.md` — the workflow rules, including the test-first gate and "proving red".

A test with no `TC-NN` in an approved `test-plan.md` does not get written.

## Credentials

There are none. Every spec seeds its own account via `POST /api/createAccount` (the
`seededAccount` fixture) and deletes it in teardown, including on failure. Never introduce
a shared `.env` credential or a `test.skip` when data is missing.

## Commands

`npm test`, `npm run test:ui`, `npm run test:api`, `npm run test:headed`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run format`, `npm run spec:validate`.
